{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "task_family": "incremental_english_modern_japanese_overlay",
  "book_id": "kinkakuji",
  "chunk_id": "kinkakuji-chunk-0558",
  "units": [
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00558",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "人们也许会认为不借助镜子就看不见自己，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "People may think that without the help of a mirror one cannot see oneself,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00558",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "残疾人总是被迫在鼻子尖上挂着一面镜子。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "but a disabled person is always forced to wear a mirror hanging at the tip of his nose.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00558",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "这面镜子昼夜都映现着我的全身。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "This mirror reflects my whole body day and night.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00558",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "不可能忘却。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "It is impossible to forget.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00558",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "因此，对于我来说，人世间所说的不安，看起来类似儿戏，这是没有法子的。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Therefore, to me, what people in the world call anxiety looks like child's play, and there is nothing to be done about that.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00558",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "我没有不安。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "I have no anxiety.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00558",
      "unit_index": 7,
      "source_text": "我就是这样存在着，如同太阳、地球。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "I exist just as I am, like the sun and the earth.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00558",
      "unit_index": 8,
      "source_text": "美丽的鸟儿和丑陋的鳄鱼一样地存在着。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Beautiful birds and ugly crocodiles exist in the same way.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00558",
      "unit_index": 9,
      "source_text": "这是千真万确的。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "This is absolutely true.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00558",
      "unit_index": 10,
      "source_text": "世界宛如一座墓碑，屹立不动。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "The world stands motionless, like a gravestone.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
